  "findings": [
    "More than half of the replay rows were emitted while the combat wrapper bypassed RL for an active fallback-turn takeover.",
    "The current boolean merges changed RL proposals with no-proposal takeover actions even though only the former are candidate-callable states.",
    "Balanced override loss still gives 68.4% of its override examples to states where the candidate is not invoked.",
    "A residual or separate head trained on the same merged labels would preserve the dominant callability confound instead of isolating override learning."
  ],
